  "cards": [
    {
      "dot": "cyan",
      "title": "Physical-key layout repair",
      "items": [
        "Layout Fix uses a reverse map to find the physical key that produced each source character, then reads that slot from the target layout. It is mechanical and has no dictionary or word guessing. (README.md:28–35; layouts.js:828–869)",
        "Characters without a source-map match pass through unchanged. Auto-detect compares script-character counts as a direction heuristic; Latin layouts share the same broad range, so it is not language detection. (script.js:71–92; layouts.js:871–903)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "emerald",
      "title": "Romaji to kana rules",
      "items": [
        "The converter greedily matches 3-, 2-, then 1-letter mora from KANA_TABLE. Doubled consonants in SOKUON_CONSONANTS produce small tsu; n, nn, and n' use separate rules. (kana.js:42–99; kana-data.js:6–170)",
        "Whole-word overrides cover konnichiwa and konbanwa. Repeated vowels become the long-vowel mark in katakana; hiragana spells them out. (kana.js:14–24, 84–95; README.md:58–65)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "violet",
      "title": "Browser preferences and assets",
      "items": [
        "Both pages load the shared stylesheet and theme controller. Light and dark are stored under localStorage key 'theme'; system mode clears the key and follows the CSS media query. (index.html:7, 105–107; romaji.html:7, 90–92; theme.js:12–24, 35–46; style.css:35–40)",
        "The shared stylesheet imports Space Grotesk and JetBrains Mono from Google Fonts, so font delivery uses an external CSS request. (style.css:1; NOTICE.md:7–12)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "amber",
      "title": "Static hosting and checks",
      "items": [
        "The two pages are static browser tools and can be opened directly; there is no app build or framework in their runtime path. (README.md:15–22, 71–84)",
        "The GitHub workflow runs a Jekyll Docker build for pushes and pull requests targeting main. It contains no Pages deployment step; README documents the self-check suites separately. (.github/workflows/jekyll-docker.yml:3–19; README.md:88–95)"
      ]
    }
  ]
